  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Sierra Nevada has $2.1B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Sierra Nevada received 46 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $45M. Obligations are down 7.7% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations rose across the last six reported years, from $112M in FY21 to $2.2B in FY25, then moved to $2.1B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $2.1B. The Department of Homeland Security is a distant second, with $122K. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest NAICS market for Sierra Nevada at $1.5B, followed by All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $482M. Other notable markets include Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $116M and All Other Telecommunications at $6.7M. The dataset notes that all figures are contract obligations except the award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, and that current-year totals are partial fiscal year to date.",
